# Contribution-control integration: source map and reservation request

**Design only, same Factory owner/task, ourostack/desk#578.** Consume the [bounded Task2 acceptance](file:///Users/microsoft/.copilot/session-state/a098a18b-72b2-45a0-8cdd-a1d0a6cdd3a6/files/578-pure-task2-source-v3-disposition.txt) and [mapping reservation](file:///Users/microsoft/.copilot/session-state/a098a18b-72b2-45a0-8cdd-a1d0a6cdd3a6/files/578-integration-mapping-design-go.txt). Accepted inert policy and pure schemas are not an operational exclusion service.

**Revision v2:** addresses FIM-1/2 and the FIM-3/4 precision requests in the [full disposition](578-integration-map-v1-review-findings.txt). [Exact v1](proof-integration-design-map-20261102-v1.md), SHA256 `7c53e6387ea5b5e08f371e1a5996e951bbeb5fa86829cd62cdf94a7d7b465f5c` / 20,900 bytes, and [original pin evidence](proof-integration-source-pins-20261102-v1.json) are preserved. This is a new written review candidate, not a source grant or a discharged finding.

## Lean reading

**Poka-yoke:** unknown ownership, generation or remote effects must not become permission or healthy zero. **Flow:** extend our existing publisher and trusted validation/build path, not another queue or publisher. **Go and see:** read actual source and qualify actual authority; supplied `ok` is not authentication. Closure requires generation-consistent contribution, reconciliation and consumer projection, not just filing or a passing pure unit.

