**Read-only authority contract:** a future `src/factory/contribution-authority.js` resolves the canonical desk/person/store from the closed private request, strict marker plus matching derivation/local-facts or owned-delivery chain, native host/session equality, existing 32-byte protected secret, exact consent/intake nonce and established publisher/store qualification witness. Machine scope is secret-bound, not an account/display name. File names, a marker alone, caller functions and a maintainer bit are insufficient. Source/delivery digests remain private.

Use the held-FD, bounded/sentinel, no-follow, owner/mode/parent-currentness discipline of `readContributionPolicyFile`, but provide closed roles for existing secret/consent/marker/receipt/delivery files, not an arbitrary path escape. Missing/corrupt/linked/drifted evidence is an explicit unknown/refusal. Authority reading must neither inspect a transcript nor repair/create/rotate anything. Ordinary `readMachineSecret`, `readConsent`, `readStatus`, `readMarker`, `readDelivered` and `readLocalFacts` are **not** that adapter.

**Compatibility is separately established local authority**, not a fresh remote PR observation. Its source fingerprint and authenticated store qualification witness are rechecked for local apply; unknown PR/main observations leave otherwise-valid exclusion effective. The real qualification witness reader/storage and strict native platform support do not exist yet. Darwin policy read calls `/bin/ls` for ACL verification; Windows strict policy read explicitly refuses. Neither is qualified by Linux-mode source tests.

